  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A photograph of a Japanese garden in autumn where the pink foliage of a tree has been redrawn as a dense cluster of small pink, peach and cream cartoon creatures with eyes and ears, beside real green maple leaves, labelled SP 45 2024.",
    "description": "A portrait format digital piece on a photograph inside a white border, captioned SP 45 2024 at lower left and MATT CRUMP at lower right. A large tree at centre has its left side canopy replaced by a dense mass of small cartoon creatures in pink, salmon, peach, cream, grey and a few blue, each with an eye, ears or a beak, packed together like leaves, with black outlines. The right side of the canopy is real green and yellow Japanese maple foliage. Below, a dark trunk, a small wooden shrine or gate structure at left, a gravel path, mown grass banks and autumn shrubs in gold and rust. The light is bright and warm.",
    "impression": "Creatures in a tree, as the caption says: the whole pink canopy is a flock, hundreds of small beings pretending to be leaves. It is the seek and find density of the Colorlands drawings landing in a photograph of a garden. From a distance it is a flowering tree; up close it is a crowd. The prettiest of the Scribbles and one of the strangest.",
